## Project Overview

This project is Part 2 of the Cybersecurity Awareness Chatbot POE. It expands the Part 1 console chatbot into a Windows Forms graphical user interface called Cybot.

Cybot helps users learn about cybersecurity topics such as passwords, phishing, scams, privacy, malware, and safe browsing.

## Part 2 Features

- Windows Forms graphical user interface
- Part 1 WAV voice greeting plays when the application opens
- Cybot branding and ASCII-style cybersecurity banner
- Personalised conversation using the user's name
- Keyword recognition for cybersecurity topics
- Random responses using `Dictionary<string, List<string>>`
- Conversation flow for follow-up questions such as “tell me more”
- Memory for the user's name, current topic, and favourite topic
- Sentiment detection for worried, curious, and frustrated messages
- Helpful handling of blank and unknown input
- Delegate used to connect chatbot responses to the GUI
- Coloured chat history with separate Cybot and user messages

## GUI Overview

The Windows Forms interface contains:

- A cybersecurity-themed Cybot banner
- A chat-history area displaying the conversation
- A text box for user input
- A Send button
- Enter-key support for sending messages
- A status message explaining supported topics

## Cybersecurity Topics Supported

Cybot can respond to questions about:

- Password safety
- Phishing
- Online scams
- Privacy
- Safe browsing
- Malware

